{
  "case_id": "2022-21-86",
  "document_hash": "1d33316ea59a3d6ffb1104d0caac78dd2565c8942db526eae146a1e5bd018774",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-86",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1d33316ea59a3d6ffb1104d0caac78dd2565c8942db526eae146a1e5bd018774",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1d33316ea59a-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:03 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Axon Enterprise, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2022-21-86",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1d33316ea59a3d6ffb1104d0caac78dd2565c8942db526eae146a1e5bd018774",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1d33316ea59a-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress has expressly granted district courts original jurisdiction over all civil actions arising under the Constitution, and it is common ground that Congress has never expressly withdrawn or restricted that jurisdiction with respect to the constitutional claims at issue here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-21-86",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1d33316ea59a3d6ffb1104d0caac78dd2565c8942db526eae146a1e5bd018774",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1d33316ea59a-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: May I ask, Mr. Clement, about the scope of your argument? Because sometimes, as you just responded to Justice Thomas's question, you're focused very specifically on the constitutional claims at issue in this case, and, in particular, the Thunder Basin analysis lends itself to that kind of focus."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Axon Enterprise, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2022-21-86",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1d33316ea59a3d6ffb1104d0caac78dd2565c8942db526eae146a1e5bd018774",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1d33316ea59a-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So, Justice Kagan, I'm really arguing to win this case on the Thunder Basin factors. That seems to be the straightforward way to win the case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-86",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1d33316ea59a3d6ffb1104d0caac78dd2565c8942db526eae146a1e5bd018774",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1d33316ea59a-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Counsel, almost any administrative process could be called collateral on constitutional issues, whether it's tax review, as in Elgin, or it's immigration issues. All of those petitioners are required to go through administrative processes, despite the fact that most of those agencies can't reach constitutional issues."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-21-86",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1d33316ea59a3d6ffb1104d0caac78dd2565c8942db526eae146a1e5bd018774",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1d33316ea59a-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: And -- and your distinction of Elgin I want to explore briefly. So, if you were bringing a claim challenging the constitutionality of the statute that was being investigated or -- or the basis for the investigation/enforcement action, you couldn't -- or what's your answer to whether you could bring a challenge like that in district court?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-21-86",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1d33316ea59a3d6ffb1104d0caac78dd2565c8942db526eae146a1e5bd018774",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1d33316ea59a-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: So let me stop you there. \"Procedures\" concerns me because I think that could be wildly open-ended and presents some of the problems that the Chief Justice and others were pointing out. So respond to that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-21-86",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1d33316ea59a3d6ffb1104d0caac78dd2565c8942db526eae146a1e5bd018774",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1d33316ea59a-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: So can I ask just on the -- the actual challenge that you've brought,"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-86",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1d33316ea59a3d6ffb1104d0caac78dd2565c8942db526eae146a1e5bd018774",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1d33316ea59a-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Textual maybe? How about that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-86",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1d33316ea59a3d6ffb1104d0caac78dd2565c8942db526eae146a1e5bd018774",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1d33316ea59a-0001-0010",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: Yes. Mr. Clement, did I misunderstand you to say that your client has not received a cease -- cease-and-desist order? Is there such an order at -- at issue here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-21-86",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1d33316ea59a3d6ffb1104d0caac78dd2565c8942db526eae146a1e5bd018774",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1d33316ea59a-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Would you at least give us your clearest textual argument?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-86",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1d33316ea59a3d6ffb1104d0caac78dd2565c8942db526eae146a1e5bd018774",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1d33316ea59a-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: So, if I understand your -- your answer, and I'm sorry to interrupt you, but I -- I just want to make sure I understand, 1331 grants jurisdiction to district courts. The FTC Act grants jurisdiction to courts of appeals for cease-and-desist orders. There's no withdrawal jurisdiction anywhere in the -- those statutes, and so you ask us to turn to the APA to discern that. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2022-21-86",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1d33316ea59a3d6ffb1104d0caac78dd2565c8942db526eae146a1e5bd018774",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1d33316ea59a-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Doesn't Free Enterprise stand as a pretty insurmountable barrier to your argument?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-86",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1d33316ea59a3d6ffb1104d0caac78dd2565c8942db526eae146a1e5bd018774",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1d33316ea59a-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Sure. Then it has no review. So what does the word \"meaningful\" add to it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-86",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1d33316ea59a3d6ffb1104d0caac78dd2565c8942db526eae146a1e5bd018774",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1d33316ea59a-0003-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And the district court said no, and the question was, is that immediately appealable under the collateral order doctrine? And the Court said no collateral order review, that if these materials are introduced at trial and that's later determined to be error, you can get vacatur of the judgment and that's good enough."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-86",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1d33316ea59a3d6ffb1104d0caac78dd2565c8942db526eae146a1e5bd018774",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1d33316ea59a-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Let me ask a question that -- that is simplistic perhaps. What sense does it make for a claim that goes to the very structure of the agency having to go through the administrative process?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Axon",
      "case_id": "2022-21-86",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "1d33316ea59a3d6ffb1104d0caac78dd2565c8942db526eae146a1e5bd018774",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1d33316ea59a-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the prime argument as to why review at the end of the day wouldn't be adequate is that it wouldn't save them from the burdens of the proceeding. They would still get review only after having gone through the ALJ and Commission adjudication."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-86",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1d33316ea59a3d6ffb1104d0caac78dd2565c8942db526eae146a1e5bd018774",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1d33316ea59a-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Isn't that a little awkward, though, that we -- we would think that the APA or -- or whatever precludes 1331 jurisdiction to resolve these claims, but it doesn't preclude All Writs Act jurisdiction in the district court to -- to -- to bring these claims? I mean --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-86",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1d33316ea59a3d6ffb1104d0caac78dd2565c8942db526eae146a1e5bd018774",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1d33316ea59a-0003-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 81,
        "start": 81
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: On the Thunder Bay factors, does Axon have to win on all three, do you have to win on all three, or is the appropriate course to balance how they --how they end up?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-86",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1d33316ea59a3d6ffb1104d0caac78dd2565c8942db526eae146a1e5bd018774",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1d33316ea59a-0003-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 82,
        "start": 82
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Okay. Suppose they lose on the first factor but win on the other two. What happens?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-86",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1d33316ea59a3d6ffb1104d0caac78dd2565c8942db526eae146a1e5bd018774",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1d33316ea59a-0003-0010",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 84,
        "start": 84
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mathews versus Eldridge dealt with a very specific fact pattern: In -- individuals who had been receiving Social Security disability benefits were informed that they were -- that the relevant agency considered them no longer to be disabled, and, therefore, their benefits would be terminated."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-86",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1d33316ea59a3d6ffb1104d0caac78dd2565c8942db526eae146a1e5bd018774",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1d33316ea59a-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 85,
        "start": 85
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I think that there are three claims, constitutional claims, here. One is the removal. And I really -- whether or not they like the double renewal or not, that they could advise us about that. In an adjudication, that's a pure legal question,"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2022-21-86",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1d33316ea59a3d6ffb1104d0caac78dd2565c8942db526eae146a1e5bd018774",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1d33316ea59a-0004-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 99,
        "start": 99
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted. (Whereupon, at 11:34 a.m., the case was submitted.)"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2022-21-86",
